<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#field-artillery">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Field artillery</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as cannon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Field artillery refers to mobile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannon">cannon</a> used on the battlefield. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">Gunpowder</a> artillery transformed warfare from the fifteenth century, giving decisive advantages to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, whose cannon at Panipat helped defeat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>. Its absence or limited use disadvantaged states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> against better-armed invaders.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Nader made systematic use of musket-armed troops, the jazayerchis or jezzailchis, and of mobile <b>field artillery</b>, including swivel guns carried by camels (zamburaks), integrating firepower with his formidable cavalry.</blockquote><a href="/empire/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1473 Mehmed II marched east; after an initial Aq Qoyunlu success on the Euphrates, the Ottoman army, with its janissaries and <b>field artillery</b>, defeated Uzun Hasan decisively at the Battle of Otlukbeli on 11 August 1473.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>He built a large standing force that combined fast cavalry, infantry trained in European drill with the help of French officers, <b>field artillery</b> and a rocket corps.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-mysore-1399-1799">Kingdom of Mysore (1399-1799) · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Gustav II Adolf built an army of conscripted peasant soldiers with mobile <b>field artillery</b> and flexible tactics.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>His use of <b>field artillery</b> and mobile cavalry tactics marked a decisive shift in Indian warfare, enabling him to overcome numerically superior forces.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
